00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.480
Because ML scales better
than those handcrafted rules

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.630
and it lets you layer models
on top of your existing logic,

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.020
you can now also delight folks
who are unlike your main user

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.370
contingent.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.460
Now, of course, what makes
all this tick is data.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.040
You can think of ML as turning
that rules-based process

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.040
on its head.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.010
Instead of starting
with the model or rules,

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:31.030
flip it to start with your data.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:34.130
Thirdly, design systems
with the expectation

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:37.190
that you will have more,
more, more data next year.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.139
Your world isn't static,
and you should expect

00:01:39.139 --> 00:01:40.180
that your data will grow.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.872
And this is a great thing
because more data wins.

00:01:42.872 --> 00:01:44.330
But what happens
when this puts you

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.450
